  {
    "id" : "constant-naming",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Constant Naming Convention",
    "description" : "This rule enforces that global constants follow either UpperCamelCase or lowerCamelCase naming conventions, while local constants should follow lowerCamelCase.",
    "explanation" : "### [constant-naming](https://github.com/sleekbyte/tailor/issues/12)\nGlobal constants should follow either *UpperCamelCase* or *lowerCamelCase* naming conventions. Local constants should follow *lowerCamelCase* naming conventions.\n\n*Preferred*\n\n```\nlet MaxHeight = 42\nlet maxHeight = 42\n```\n\n*Not Preferred*\n\n```\nlet max_height = 42\n```",
    "enabled" : true,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
