  },
  {
    "id" : "lower-camel-case",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce lowerCamelCase Naming Convention",
    "description" : "This rule enforces the use of lowerCamelCase naming convention for method and variable names.",
    "explanation" : "### [lower-camel-case](https://github.com/sleekbyte/tailor/issues/9)\n`method` and `var` names should follow *lowerCamelCase* naming convention: first letter of the entire word is lowercase, but subsequent first letters are uppercase.\n#### Method and selector names\n*Preferred*\n\n```\nfunc someMethod() {\n\t// method definition goes here\n}\n```\n\n*Not Preferred*\n\n```\nfunc some-method() {\n\t// method definition goes here\n}\n```\n\n#### Variable names\n*Preferred*\n\n```\nvar someVariable = someValue\n```\n\n*Not Preferred*\n\n```\nvar Some_Var1able = someValue\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "max-class-length",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "Complexity",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Maximum Class Length",
    "description" : "This rule enforces a maximum line limit on the length of class bodies to ensure classes do not become excessively long.",
    "explanation" : "### [max-class-length](https://github.com/sleekbyte/tailor/issues/14)\nEnforce a line limit on the lengths of class bodies.\n\n```\ntailor [--max-class-length <x>]\n```\n\nFor example, limiting classes to 2 lines would trigger a violation for the following 3 line class:\n\n```\n1 class ThreeLineClass {\n2     // This class spans from lines 1-4.\n3\n4 }\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 15,
    "parameters" : [
      {
        "name" : "max-class-length",
        "default" : "30",
        "description" : "Maximum length of class bodies"
      }
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "max-closure-length",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Maximum Length on Closure Bodies",
    "description" : "This rule enforces a maximum line limit on the length of closure bodies to keep them concise and readable.",
    "explanation" : "### [max-closure-length](https://github.com/sleekbyte/tailor/issues/14)\nEnforce a line limit on the lengths of closure bodies.\n\n```\ntailor [--max-closure-length <x>]\n```\n\nFor example, limiting closures to 2 lines would trigger a violation for the following 3 line closure:\n\n```\n1 reversed = names.sort({ (s1: String, s2: String) -> Bool in\n2     // This closure spans from lines 1-4.\n3     return s1 > s2\n4 })\n```",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
      {
        "name" : "max-closure-length",
        "default" : "5",
        "description" : "Maximum length of closure bodies"
      }
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
